{"id":"CVE-2009-0606","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2009-02-17T17:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T04:40:05.010Z","description":"The link_image function in linker/linker.c in the dynamic linker in Bionic in Open Handset Alliance Android 1.0 on the T-Mobile G1 phone does not properly handle file descriptors 0, 1, and 2 for a setgid program, which allows local users to create arbitrary files owned by certain groups, possibly a related issue to CVE-2002-0820.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/48840","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"android-dynamic-linker-privilege-escalation(48840)"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/33695","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"33695"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/500753/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20090208 rooting your own phone: android security"}],"vendors":["android"]}
{"id":"CVE-2009-0607","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2009-02-17T17:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T04:40:04.984Z","description":"Multiple integer overflows in malloc_leak.c in Bionic in Open Handset Alliance Android 1.0 have unknown impact and attack vectors, related to the (1) chk_calloc and (2) leak_calloc functions.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/33695","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"33695"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/500753/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20090208 rooting your own phone: android security"},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/48841","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"android-malloc-overflow(48841)"}],"vendors":["android"]}
{"id":"CVE-2009-0608","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2009-02-17T17:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T04:40:04.247Z","description":"Integer overflow in the showLog function in fake_log_device.c in liblog in Open Handset Alliance Android 1.0 allows attackers to trigger a buffer overflow and possibly have unspecified other impact by sending a large number of input lines.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/33695","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"33695"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/500753/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20090208 rooting your own phone: android security"},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/48842","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"android-showlog-bo(48842)"}],"vendors":["android"]}
{"id":"CVE-2009-1442","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2009-05-07T17:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T05:13:25.631Z","description":"Multiple integer overflows in Skia, as used in Google Chrome 1.x before 1.0.154.64 and 2.x, and possibly Android, might allow remote attackers to execute arbitrary code in the renderer process via a crafted (1) image or (2) canvas.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://code.google.com/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=10736","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2009/1266","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2009-1266"},{"url":"http://googlechromereleases.blogspot.com/2009/05/stable-update-security-fix.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/35014","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"35014"},{"url":"http://osvdb.org/54248","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_OSVDB"],"name":"54248"},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id?1022175","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1022175"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/34859","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"34859"},{"url":"http://code.google.com/p/skia/source/detail?r=159","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["android","google-chrome"]}
{"id":"CVE-2009-1754","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2009-05-26T15:16:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T05:27:54.258Z","description":"The PackageManagerService class in services/java/com/android/server/PackageManagerService.java in Android 1.5 through 1.5 CRB42 does not properly check developer certificates during processing of sharedUserId requests at an application's installation time, which allows remote user-assisted attackers to access application data by creating a package that specifies a shared user ID with an arbitrary application.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/35090","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"35090"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2009/05/22/14","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20090522 [oCERT-2009-006] Android improper package verification when using shared uids"},{"url":"http://www.ocert.org/advisories/ocert-2009-006.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/503770","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20090522 [oCERT-2009-006] Android improper package verification when using shared uids"},{"url":"http://android.git.kernel.org/?p=platform/frameworks/base.git%3Ba=commit%3Bh=5d6d773fab559fdc12e553d60d789f3991ac552c","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["android"]}
{"id":"CVE-2009-2348","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2009-07-17T16:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T05:44:56.000Z","description":"Android 1.5 CRBxx allows local users to bypass the (1) Manifest.permission.CAMERA (aka android.permission.CAMERA) and (2) Manifest.permission.AUDIO_RECORD (aka android.permission.RECORD_AUDIO) configuration settings by installing and executing an application that does not make a permission request before using the camera or microphone.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://android.git.kernel.org/?p=platform/packages/apps/Camera.git%3Ba=commit%3Bh=e655d54160e5a56d4909f2459eeae9012e9f187f","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://android.git.kernel.org/?p=platform/frameworks/base.git%3Ba=commit%3Bh=7b7225c8fdbead25235c74811b30ff4ee690dc58","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/51798","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"android-permission-security-bypass(51798)"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/505012/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20090716 [oCERT-2009-011] Android improper camera and audio permission verification"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2009/07/16/4","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20090716 [oCERT-2009-011] Android improper camera and audio permission verification"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/35717","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"35717"},{"url":"http://android.git.kernel.org/?p=platform/frameworks/base.git%3Ba=commit%3Bh=4d8adefd35efdea849611b8b02d61f9517e47760","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.ocert.org/advisories/ocert-2009-011.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["android"]}
{"id":"CVE-2009-2656","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2009-08-03T18:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T05:59:56.189Z","description":"Unspecified vulnerability in the com.android.phone process in Android 1.0, 1.1, and 1.5 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (network disconnection) via a crafted SMS message, as demonstrated by Collin Mulliner and Charlie Miller at Black Hat USA 2009.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.blackhat.com/presentations/bh-usa-09/MILLER/BHUSA09-Miller-FuzzingPhone-PAPER.pdf","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/35886","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"35886"},{"url":"http://osvdb.org/56750","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_OSVDB"],"name":"56750"}],"vendors":["android"]}
